                            <comment id="504091" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:58:45 +0000">&lt;p&gt;parallel-scale-nfsv3 test_connectathon (Rainshadow, 2026-09-22 to 2026-10-21): 89 enforced failures, all on lustre-master and lustre-master-next full-part-2, ~20% of runs, all ldiskfs. Every failing session is an interop run (master servers, b2_15 or b2_16 clients, e.g. lustre-master-next-el10.2_lustre-b2_15-el9.6 session 595cc7e4-d8e4-4ba6-87de-091d50d2df24); none on master/master or review patches. Failure is the LOCKING tests: 'Test #1 ... F_TEST FAILED, errno=37 (ENOLCK)'. Master already skips this test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-18649" title="parallel-scale-nfsv3 test_connectathon: lock tests failed" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-18649"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-18649&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, commit 0543fc4eb4), but interop runs use the older branch's parallel-scale-nfsv3.sh, and b2_15/b2_16 do not have the skip (suite log shows only 'excepting tests: racer_on_nfs'). Backports of the skip: b2_16 &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69896" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69896&lt;/a&gt; and b2_15 &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69897" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69897&lt;/a&gt;. This hides the ENOLCK on NFSv3 locking rather than fixing it; the underlying cause is not established. nfsv4 connectathon passes in the same interop configs.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
